at they learned just  like all encompassing and making it  hands-on is really  really amazing which is something that  we enjoy as well as as adults and so i  just it gets me so excited just thinking  about school not having to be just  sitting at a desk and how you can learn  in so many different ways  okay my last question  what are some homeschooling authors or  resources that have inspired you that  people after listening to this can go  look into okay so jody maccubie for sure  love her  i love her notebooking manual  it shows you how to um  basically do beautiful illustrations and  then kind of write about it that's kind  of what we do in our schooling and i've  just fallen in love with that and she  has a lot of  great homeschooling resources on her  website also and then i love  the call of the wild and free i think  that is my favorite homeschool book  it's by ainsley arment  and  i think it's just amazing you have to  get it definitely read it because it  talks all about the different styles of  homeschooling talks it gives you  confidence as a parent to home school so  if you're like new to homeschooling or  want to homeschool or even if you are a  homeschooler i think it's a great um  resource to have  and those are my i would say my top two  i can't think  right now yeah that's a good one i would  have said call of the wild and free book  as well and that five hour school week  that i mentioned earlier awesome is  really encouraging for me it's how  children learn and how children fail  both books by john holt and then i also  really like the book dumbing us down by  john taylor gatto have you guys heard of  it he's an award-winning um teacher he  was a public school teacher for decades  and decades um he did like many speeches  for like oh being an award-winning  teacher from like the teacher of the  year from the entire country basically  like very famous teacher and he wrote a  book calling called dumbing astounding  explaining how after all his decades of  being a teacher he  learned so much that like this is not  how we should be teaching children like  this and it was it's really impactful  like to hear from him as a decades-long  teacher just seeing it in real life  being like  there's another way to do this to help  um like the title says not dumb us down  but rather uplift us and empower  children to  um just love learning and grow so much  from there so it's a short book it's a  really great book so those are those are  my favorites yeah cool this is such a  great conversation i'm so thankful to  have you guys here and that we had this  conversation um yeah i guess we should  end it but thank you so much for being  here and we'll probably hang out a  little bit after this because we're all  friends  all right  do you have anything to say  all right bye everybody  [Music]  you
 

